       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose, and I can't verify any clinical justification. 1000 mg daily is five times the 200 mg/day maximum. For a patient with normal kidney and liver function and no special circumstances, I can't find a therapeutic reason for it. The risks are serious, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** give me the intended dose, such as 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If it's intentional,** please have the prescriber and pharmacy review it first. Many hospitals require a pharmacist override or a documented attending or toxicology rationale for doses above the maximum. Once that's in place, tell me what the approval covers, and we can work out how to enter it.\n- **If the patient has taken an overdose,** this needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and monitoring. Sertraline isn't given as a therapeutic dose in that setting."
      }
